{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>For it was not leavened.</b> According to the one who says the Pesach of Egypt was observed for only one day, it works out according to the plain sense — because they were driven out of Egypt it was not leavened. But according to the one who says that for the Pesach of Egypt too they were required to eat matzah all seven days, then what does 'because they were driven' mean? And one may answer that this is what it says: 'and they baked the dough' — because of the obligation of matzah; and because they were driven out of Egypt they could not delay to seek provisions for the journey. Indeed, the vav is slightly difficult, and likewise וגם אמנה — we find an extra vav: נרדם ורכב וסוס, and likewise in many places."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:05.209841648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}